dummy head head-related impulse responses), Copyright 2018 University of York, AudioLab,
Department of Electronic Engineering, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
(tools/hrtf/LICENSE-Apache-2.0.txt, http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0).
https://www.york.ac.uk/sadie-project/database.html
C. Armstrong, L. Thresh, D. Murphy, G. Kearney, "A Perceptual Evaluation of Individual and
Non-Individual HRTFs: A Case Study of the SADIE II Database", Applied Sciences 8(11):2029,
2018, https://doi.org/10.3390/app8112029

The data was modified: five speaker directions (0, +/-30, +/-110 degrees) were taken,
averaged for a symmetric head, rebuilt as minimum-phase filters with a far-ear delay,
shortened to 32, 64 and 128 taps, combined into sum and difference filters, scaled and
quantised to 16 bits. The result is the headphone surround table xbox360/surround_tab.h,
compiled into xw.xex. tools/hrtf/CREDITS.txt describes each step; tools/hrtf/gen.py does
them.
